import{_ as t,o as s,c as o,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.BN3Eol-0.js";const g=JSON.parse(`{"title":"PRD-038 · Glossary: the site's technical terms, one sentence each","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"prd/PRD-038.md","filePath":"prd/PRD-038.md"}`),r={name:"prd/PRD-038.md"};function i(n,e,l,c,d,h){return s(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="prd-038-·-glossary-the-site-s-technical-terms-one-sentence-each" tabindex="-1">PRD-038 · Glossary: the site&#39;s technical terms, one sentence each <a class="header-anchor" href="#prd-038-·-glossary-the-site-s-technical-terms-one-sentence-each" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;PRD-038 · Glossary: the site&#39;s technical terms, one sentence each&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Status · Shipped on <code>tech-debt/phases</code> (2026-10-31), plan approved by the operator in session; §5 term links shipped on <code>tech-debt/0.9.6</code> (2026-11-04) Date · 2026-10-31 Owner · Marko Builds on · <code>scripts/i18n-tools/native-terms.json</code> (<code>term</code> section, the space-terms pilot) · <code>git show 5cf9491e398:docs/wip/2026-10-31-space-terms-glossary-pilot.md</code> · <code>/sourcing</code> (a small data-driven page) · PRD-037 (the sibling page for names) · RFC-011 OQ-4 (the deferred A–Z science lookup)</p></blockquote><blockquote><p><strong>Why this is a PRD.</strong> It adds a public route built from an internal translation tool. It promises readers one word per term on every page, and the term gate in CI keeps that promise.</p></blockquote><h2 id="_1-·-what" tabindex="-1">1 · What <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-·-what" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;1 · What&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>/science/glossary</code>: a page like the glossary at the back of a technical book. For every technical term in the glossary&#39;s <code>term</code> section (20 at launch: orbit, trajectory, burn, flyby, orbit insertion …), in the reader&#39;s language:</p><ul><li>the term, sorted alphabetically in that language;</li><li>a one-sentence definition;</li><li><strong>Read more:</strong> the /science page that explains it (18 of 20; rendezvous and payload have none);</li><li><strong>Used on:</strong> the pages that use the term most (up to 5).</li></ul><p>Each entry has an anchor (<code>/science/glossary#gravity-assist</code>) for deep links.</p><p><strong>Where it lives:</strong> a &quot;see also&quot; tab of /science, next to Reading List and Watch List (operator, 2026-10-31). The terms are the science section&#39;s vocabulary: every definition but two points to a science article, and the articles mostly explain these terms. Missions, fleet and essays use them without explaining them, and the &quot;used on&quot; links show that use. Also linked from the footer, the phone drawer and the end of the /science landing.</p><h2 id="_2-·-data-path" tabindex="-1">2 · Data path <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-·-data-path" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2 · Data path&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Terms and forms:</strong> <code>native-terms.json</code> <code>term</code> (binding form per locale; <code>_read_more</code> names the science page).</li><li><strong>Definitions:</strong> overlays <code>i18n-src/&lt;locale&gt;/glossary/terms.json</code>, translated like any overlay. They are checked by <code>problems()</code> and by the term gate, so the definitions use the binding forms. They live in their own i18n chunk (<code>glossary</code>), so no other page loads them.</li><li><strong>Build:</strong> <code>scripts/build-glossary.mjs</code> (in <code>npm run build</code>) writes <code>static/data/glossary/&lt;locale&gt;.json</code>, one file per locale. It resolves names, definitions, the read-more page and the &quot;used on&quot; pages with their titles. &quot;Used on&quot; is counted on the English text, the way <code>term-drift.mjs</code> finds a term. The output is generated and gitignored.</li><li><strong>A term added</strong> to the glossary (with its definitions) appears on the page; no code change.</li></ul><h2 id="_3-·-guards" tabindex="-1">3 · Guards <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-·-guards" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;3 · Guards&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>scripts/build-glossary.test.ts</code>: <ul><li>every term has a definition in all 14 locales (no English fallback) and a title for every linked page;</li><li>the science, essay and program links exist;</li><li>the route mapping is tested.</li></ul></li><li>The term gate (<code>term-glossary.test.ts</code>) covers the definitions (<code>glossary</code> tree).</li><li><code>check-internal-links</code> (build) checks every rendered link, and the a11y gate includes <code>/science/glossary</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="_4-·-relation-to-other-pages" tabindex="-1">4 · Relation to other pages <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-·-relation-to-other-pages" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;4 · Relation to other pages&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>PRD-037 (<code>/names</code>, draft):</strong> the same glossary file, for names. Separate pages, because names and terms follow different rules (origin rule vs. native terms).</li><li><strong>RFC-011 OQ-4:</strong> the deferred alphabetical science lookup. <code>/science/glossary</code> covers the technical vocabulary, and each entry links to its science page. A flat <code>/science/all</code> list of every section is still not built.</li></ul><h2 id="_5-·-terms-linked-from-the-text-shipped-2026-11-04-0-9-6" tabindex="-1">5 · Terms linked from the text (shipped 2026-11-04, 0.9.6) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-·-terms-linked-from-the-text-shipped-2026-11-04-0-9-6" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5 · Terms linked from the text (shipped 2026-11-04, 0.9.6)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In /science articles the first mention of a glossary term links to its entry (<code>/science/glossary#gravity-assist</code>), closing the loop in both directions. Rules (operator, 2026-11-04: at most 2 per paragraph, a quiet link):</p><ul><li><strong>Where:</strong> the 101 narrative and the body paragraphs, in reading order. Not the title, the lede, captions or formula captions. Essays, missions and fleet are not linked yet.</li><li><strong>How often:</strong> each term once per article, at its first mention; at most 2 term links per paragraph, and a term crowded out moves to its next mention.</li><li><strong>Never:</strong> on the term&#39;s own read-more article; inside an author&#39;s <code>[text](link)</code>; on pages where <code>_en_skip</code> gives the word another sense (the Shuttle &quot;orbiter&quot;).</li><li><strong>Which words:</strong> a mention counts where the term gate would see it: the English of the same field uses the term, and the locale&#39;s text matches the glossary&#39;s stems (inflections, Korean particles, Arabic clitics included). In scripts with spaces the link covers the whole word, up to 4 letters beyond the stem (an ending, never a compound: de «Nutzlastspezialisten» is not linked as &quot;payload&quot;). The word must share a piece of the binding form (3 letters, 2 in ja / zh-CN / ko), so a plain word the gate accepts (ja 探査機 &quot;probe&quot; for orbiter) is not linked; a word that is more another term&#39;s (es «orbitador», ja 軌道 where the paragraph also says &quot;trajectory&quot;) is skipped.</li><li><strong>Look:</strong> the word keeps the body colour with a dotted teal underline; solid on hover and focus.</li></ul><p><strong>Data path:</strong> <code>scripts/glossary-links.mjs</code> (called by <code>build-glossary.mjs</code>) writes <code>static/data/glossary/&lt;locale&gt;.links.json</code>: per article, per paragraph, <code>[term id, offset in the plain text, text]</code>. The article&#39;s load reads it; <code>parseInline(para, terms)</code> in <code>src/lib/science-inline.ts</code> links a term only where its text still sits at that offset, so an overlay edited after the build loses the link instead of getting a wrong one. About 30 KB per locale, not precached; ~480–580 links per locale on 168 articles (median 3 per article).</p><p><strong>Guards:</strong> <code>scripts/glossary-links.test.ts</code> (the rules, mutation-checked: lifting the compound limit fails it), <code>src/lib/science-inline.test.ts</code> (offsets, author links, moved text), <code>build-glossary</code> problems (every link&#39;s text sits at its offset; every term id exists), <code>tests/e2e/science.spec.ts</code> (en, de, ar: a term link lands on its entry; once per article; not on its own page).</p><h2 id="_5b-·-later-still-a-small-visual-per-term-operator-idea-2026-10-31" tabindex="-1">5b · Later still: a small visual per term (operator idea, 2026-10-31) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5b-·-later-still-a-small-visual-per-term-operator-idea-2026-10-31" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5b · Later still: a small visual per term (operator idea, 2026-10-31)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After the term links, the final item. Each entry gets a small visual in the style of the science pages&#39; diagrams, because a picture helps with the concept: apogee/perigee on an ellipse, a burn as a thrust arrow on an orbit, a gravity-assist bend, staging, the entry corridor. It uses the house pipeline in <code>docs/guides/diagram-art-style.md</code> (precise SVG sketch → Higgsfield <code>nano_banana_pro</code> → webp) so the glossary and /science read as one hand, and it reuses a science page&#39;s diagram where one already shows the term. Generation spends Higgsfield credits: count the terms, estimate the credits and get a go before running.</p><h2 id="_6-·-non-goals" tabindex="-1">6 · Non-goals <a class="header-anchor" href="#_6-·-non-goals" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;6 · Non-goals&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Definitions for every science page.</strong> Only the glossary&#39;s terms appear here.</li><li><strong>Search on the page:</strong> 20 entries; site search (Cmd-K) covers lookup. Revisit at ~100 terms, and add an A–Z jump bar then too.</li><li><strong>Per-locale &quot;used on&quot; counts:</strong> the pages are the same in every locale, so the counts come from the English text.</li></ul>',23)])])}const m=t(r,[["render",i]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
